WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:07.510
29. Say hello to our new mechanical friends.

2
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:12.510
For years we've been hearing it. The robots are coming. The robots are coming.

3
00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:19.510
Well, the long wait is finally over. The robots are no longer coming. They're already here.

4
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.510
The robotics industry has changed economies and lifestyles around the world.

5
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:29.510
One area in which these changes are particularly obvious is manufacturing.

6
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Industrial robots, those robot arms that assemble things in factories, are becoming increasingly capable.

7
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.510
Nowadays, these robots can assemble large items like cars with very little input from human workers.

8
00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.510
They can also work 24 hours a day without ever making a mistake.

9
00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:53.510
It's no wonder that factory workers around the world are losing their jobs to robots.

10
00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.510
Of course, that's not what comes to mind when most of us think of robots.

11
00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:03.510
We imagine personal, human-like machines that can cook our food and do our laundry for us.

12
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.510
Fortunately, they're here as well.

13
00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:11.510
Tech companies are fighting tooth and nail to achieve the first big success in personal robotics.

14
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:16.510
Japan's Sharp Electronics is betting on simpler, more affordable robots.

15
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:23.510
For this reason, it has launched RoboHon, a cute little robot that functions similarly to a smartphone.

16
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.510
RoboHon can understand simple voice commands.

17
00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:31.510
It also knows some pretty sweet dance moves, which it shows off whenever it receives a phone call.

18
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:37.510
Other companies are targeting the high-end market with technologically advanced personal robots.

19
00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:41.510
Two examples are Honda's Asimo and SoftBank's Pepper.

20
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:45.510
Asimo can run, jump, and climb stairs just like a human being.

21
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:51.510
It also has sensitive hands that can perform delicate tasks like pouring a cup of coffee.

22
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.510
Pepper, on the other hand, can sense and respond to human emotions.

23
00:01:55.510 --> 00:02:00.510
This could come in handy when dealing with people who have lost their livelihoods to robots.
